    "$comment": [
        "The third-party tools an engine release is built against, pinned to exact files.",
        "A project switches a tool on; the engine then fetches EXACTLY this file, from the release mirror first,",
        "and refuses anything whose size or SHA-256 differs. Changing a pin is a deliberate act: it ships with an engine version.",
        "`upstream` is the file the vendor publishes (its URL, size and SHA-256 are what the pin means).",
        "`tools/sync-external-tools.mjs` copies it to the mirror as a .zip (the one archive format the engine reads) and",
        "publishes an index; `--record` fills a missing size or SHA-256 from the vendor's file."
